147	<section id="s1" class="part">
148	<h2>Landed since the curator&rsquo;s last approval</h2>
149	<p>Eleven items, not yet read, oldest first. The curator read items 41 and 42 at 22:23 UTC on 23 November 2026, so they went. At 00:1x UTC on 24 November the curator approved drafts 43 to 65, with the changes that he approved on their threads that evening, and they landed in one commit at 00:13 UTC. The words that he approved get no item. Each item below shows a passage whose landed words differ from them, against the approved words. In five passages, the approved words named the landing report or the gather record, both withdrawn on the drafts&rsquo; threads before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection; the coordinator and the skill writer changed each by the fewest words. In one, a word changed for the skills&rsquo; lint. Items 86 to 90 are the five passages of one later change of 24 November: when the coordinator writes the boot note.</p>
150	
151	<section id="l80" class="part item">
152	<h3><span class="num">Change 80 &middot; SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 32</span>A landed default is named in one line at the landing</h3>
153	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 44; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in.</span>
154	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 32</p>
155	<dl class="gloss"><dt>default</dt><dd>Option that stands unless the curator picks another: the one that an ask recommends, or the choice that an agent landed without the curator's word, which FACTS states and the landing <span class="cut">report</span> names <span class="cut">or counts.</span><span class="add">in one line.</span></dd></dl>
156	</div></div>
157	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words said that the landing report names or counts a landed default. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection: the post-batch review&rsquo;s section &ldquo;For the curator&rdquo; already tells him what each batch changed. So the entry now says that the landing names the default in one line, as step 2 of the landing now does for each decision that landed. The counts went with the report.</p></div>
158	</section>
159	
160	<section id="l81" class="part item">
161	<h3><span class="num">Change 81 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</span>A landed decision is named in one line at the landing, in two places</h3>
162	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 48; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
163	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</p>
164	<p>It reaches the curator in one of three ways:</p>
165	<ol start="1"><li><strong>Asked before the work.</strong> A known fork is probed, and put as an ask before the batch is briefed.</li><li><strong>Landed, then asked.</strong> A decision that can be undone lands with its default, and <span class="cut">goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">is named in one line at the landing.</span> Its question goes in the review queue, with the work that needs the answer, and stays there until the curator answers. Put the questions to the curator in the order of the work that needs them. A question that no work needs comes last.</li><li><strong>A hold.</strong> A decision that cannot be undone, or that acts against the curator's word, goes to the curator at once.</li></ol>
166	<p>Every other decision that changes the tree is closed when it lands. FACTS states it, and <span class="cut">it goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">the landing names it in one line.</span> If it lands outside a batch, name it to the curator in one line, in your next message. A rung's small decisions go in the gap ledger, as rows. None of these holds up the work. If the curator objects to a decision that landed, open a review-queue item for it, and put it as your next ask. It is not a hold.</p>
167	</div></div>
168	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words sent a landed decision into the landing report twice: in the second of the three ways, and in the paragraph after them. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection. Both places now say that the landing names the decision in one line, the line that step 2 of the landing gives each decision. The rest of the passage landed as approved.</p></div>
169	</section>
170	
171	<section id="l82" class="part item">
172	<h3><span class="num">Change 82 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the bullet on changes that wait for the curator&rsquo;s yes, its first sentence, line 126</span>The landing&rsquo;s one line for each decision waits for the curator&rsquo;s yes</h3>
173	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 49; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
174	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the bullet on changes that wait for the curator&rsquo;s yes, its first sentence, line 126</p>
175	<ul><li>A change that touches the curator's role and decisions (this section), the asks, the held list, the review queue, the <span class="cut">landing report</span><span class="add">landing's one line for each decision</span> or the register in which you write to the curator (the bullets at the head of "Talking to the curator") waits for the curator's yes to its exact words.</li></ul>
176	</div></div>
177	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words listed the landing report among the things whose change waits for the curator&rsquo;s yes. With the report withdrawn before the landing, the list names what took its place: the landing&rsquo;s one line for each decision, step 2 of the landing.</p></div>
178	</section>
179	
180	<section id="l83" class="part item">
181	<h3><span class="num">Change 83 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;The go&rdquo;, the third bullet, line 39</span>One word for the skills&rsquo; lint: &ldquo;the batch&rdquo;</h3>
182	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 60; struck through, the approved word that went; underlined, the word that came in.</span>
183	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;The go&rdquo;, the third bullet, line 39</p>
184	<ul><li>If a question that the batch record raises is consequential (<code>SKILL.md</code>), put it to the curator first. Otherwise decide it. While the curator is away, overnight, take a consequential question's recommended default, and launch. Its question goes in the review queue, with <span class="cut">this</span><span class="add">the</span> batch as the work that needs it. If that default would reverse a decision of the curator, hold that batch, and launch the repair batch (<code>explorations/coordinator/REPAIR-BATCH.md</code>) in its place.</li></ul>
185	</div></div>
186	<div class="note"><p><strong>A word that goes stale.</strong> The skills&rsquo; lint flags &ldquo;this batch&rdquo; as wording that goes stale, since a skill outlives any one batch. The skill writer changed one word: the bullet now says &ldquo;the batch&rdquo;, the batch whose record raised the question. The rule does not change.</p></div>
187	</section>
188	
189	<section id="l84" class="part item">
190	<h3><span class="num">Change 84 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;The roles&rdquo;, the third bullet, its sentences on a reserved point and a file outside the rung&rsquo;s section, line 55</span>A file outside a rung&rsquo;s section is listed in the post-batch review</h3>
191	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 61; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in.</span>
192	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;The roles&rdquo;, the third bullet, its sentences on a reserved point and a file outside the rung&rsquo;s section, line 55</p>
193	<p>Reaching a reserved point, or a file outside what the rung's section of the batch record names, does not make a settled fix contested: it lands. The point goes where "Reserved points and repairs" says, and the <span class="cut">gather record</span><span class="add">post-batch review's section "For the curator"</span> lists the file.</p>
194	</div></div>
195	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn term.</strong> The approved words had the gather record list a file that a rung changed outside its section of the batch record. The curator asked what the gather record was for, and its new glossary entry was withdrawn before the landing, since no rule needed the name. So the sentence now has the post-batch review list the file, in its section &ldquo;For the curator&rdquo;, where the curator reads what each batch changed.</p></div>
196	</section>
197	
198	<section id="l85" class="part item">
199	<h3><span class="num">Change 85 &middot; references/batch.md, &ldquo;Reserved points and repairs&rdquo;, the first bullet, line 69</span>A reversible reserved point is named in one line at the landing</h3>
200	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 63; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. The third bullet of draft 63 landed as approved.</span>
201	<p class="where-in">references/batch.md, &ldquo;Reserved points and repairs&rdquo;, the first bullet, line 69</p>
202	<ul><li>A reversible reserved point does not hold the batch. The batch lands with the point's default, and the point <span class="cut">goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">is named in one line at the landing.</span> If the point is consequential, such as a line of microGPT, its question also goes in the review queue. A point that is no decision, such as an output that a rung cannot explain, becomes a ledger row.</li></ul>
203	</div></div>
204	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words put a reversible reserved point in the landing report. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection. The point is now named in one line at the landing, as every decision that landed is. The rest of the bullet landed as approved: a consequential point also has its question in the review queue, and a point that is no decision becomes a ledger row.</p></div>
205	</section>
206	
207	<section id="l86" class="part item">
208	<h3><span class="num">Change 86 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The boot&rdquo;, the bullet on the boot note, line 264</span>The boot note is written for a reader without the context, and rewritten at a compaction ask</h3>
209	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the text before commit <code>906bf0c81a</code>; struck through, the words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
210	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The boot&rdquo;, the bullet on the boot note, line 264</p>
211	<ul><li><span class="add">Your context survives a process stop. Write the boot note only for a reader without it: a later session, or a worker, for a line that a rule of this skill names. Commit each write.</span> Rewrite the <span class="cut">boot</span> note whole <span class="cut">at every change. Never append to it.</span><span class="add">near the context's limit, before another session takes over, and before you answer a compaction ask. If the curator did not ask, tell them.</span></li></ul>
212	</div></div>
