154	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, glossary, &ldquo;default&rdquo;, line 32</p>
155	<dl class="gloss"><dt>default</dt><dd>Option that stands unless the curator picks another: the one that an ask recommends, or the choice that an agent landed without the curator's word, which FACTS states and the landing <span class="cut">report</span> names <span class="cut">or counts.</span><span class="add">in one line.</span></dd></dl>
156	</div></div>
157	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words said that the landing report names or counts a landed default. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection: the post-batch review&rsquo;s section &ldquo;For the curator&rdquo; already tells him what each batch changed. So the entry now says that the landing names the default in one line, as step 2 of the landing now does for each decision that landed. The counts went with the report.</p></div>
158	</section>
