161	<h3><span class="num">Change 81 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</span>A landed decision is named in one line at the landing, in two places</h3>
162	<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Landed text, against the approved words of draft 48; struck through, the approved words that went; underlined, the words that came in. In the skill&rsquo;s words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
163	<p class="where-in">SKILL.md, &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo;, the three ways and the paragraph after them, lines 103 to 109</p>
164	<p>It reaches the curator in one of three ways:</p>
165	<ol start="1"><li><strong>Asked before the work.</strong> A known fork is probed, and put as an ask before the batch is briefed.</li><li><strong>Landed, then asked.</strong> A decision that can be undone lands with its default, and <span class="cut">goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">is named in one line at the landing.</span> Its question goes in the review queue, with the work that needs the answer, and stays there until the curator answers. Put the questions to the curator in the order of the work that needs them. A question that no work needs comes last.</li><li><strong>A hold.</strong> A decision that cannot be undone, or that acts against the curator's word, goes to the curator at once.</li></ol>
166	<p>Every other decision that changes the tree is closed when it lands. FACTS states it, and <span class="cut">it goes in the landing report.</span><span class="add">the landing names it in one line.</span> If it lands outside a batch, name it to the curator in one line, in your next message. A rung's small decisions go in the gap ledger, as rows. None of these holds up the work. If the curator objects to a decision that landed, open a review-queue item for it, and put it as your next ask. It is not a hold.</p>
167	</div></div>
168	<div class="note"><p><strong>The withdrawn report.</strong> The approved words sent a landed decision into the landing report twice: in the second of the three ways, and in the paragraph after them. That report was withdrawn before the landing, at the curator&rsquo;s objection. Both places now say that the landing names the decision in one line, the line that step 2 of the landing gives each decision. The rest of the passage landed as approved.</p></div>
169	</section>
